<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cagliari</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karalis, Calaris</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cagliari is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, on its southern coast. Founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> as Karalis, it was a Roman port and then the seat of the medieval Judicate of Cagliari. The Pisans built the fortified Castello quarter in 1216, and after the Aragonese conquest in the 14th century it became the capital of the Kingdom of Sardinia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cagliari.jpg" alt="Cagliari" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nilo1926 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cagliari_collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
